 - **americas-recomp (2026-11-24): nuked.** Its repo `realdody/americas-recomp` has answered 404 since the scout's 22:04 UTC run on 2026-11-23. Its owner's account is still active, and GitHub's DMCA log (published through Nov 20 at the time) has no notice against it. The owner chose to grey it out like Leonida: the entry has a `nuked` field, so it is unranked and left out of the headline numbers. Don't remove the field or re-rank it unless the repo itself comes back; if it does, report it to the owner.
 - **Board removed (2026-11-24):** the owner took the board off the site after traffic swamped the free Supabase database (`board.html` and `assets/js/board.js` deleted; history keeps them). Skip step 5b: no moderation calls to Supabase. Its threads and posts stay in the database. View counting and the live viewer count came back the same day in a lighter form: about 1 in 5 tabs reports its views, and the count is served from `functions/api/live.js` behind Cloudflare's cache. `STATS_PAUSED` in `assets/js/config.js` still turns both off.
 - **No leaked-game images, no Discord (2026-11-24):** the owner had the site's Discord pill and its invite removed, along with two article images: CGBJ's capture from the leaked game and the Discord profile screenshot on the Marvis article. Never use a picture of the leaked game (a screenshot, capture or video frame from any build) or a Discord screenshot as an article `image`, even when it's the source's `og:image`; use `null`. Don't add any image like that to the repo, and don't link or mention a PortWatch Discord.
+- **Active private-build story ratings (2026-11-26, owner's call):** the owner rates every active private build at `story: 0.6` ("Half the story"): NotNozy, Doomsday, darkworldhm and suri. CGBJ was public briefly and is a private build again (see its entry above). This supersedes older story values and reports above. It puts NotNozy at 84.3%, the overall headline lead. Keep the story scores until the owner changes them; describe them as owner ratings when independent evidence does not establish that progress. Leave nuked omonkey's historical values untouched.
+- **Rendering re-rated (2026-11-26, owner's call):** after DexNom's call for developers (frame-rate-first builds run at low resolution with broken textures and heavy memory use), the owner capped rendering at `render: 0.7` for every build that was above it: AvatarManz, Belobug, CGBJ, Doomsday, NotNozy and suri (darkworldhm and hyphennn were already at 0.7). DexNom goes from 0.9 to `render: 0.85`, the highest on the board and the only one at "Close to the console". Doomsday's ray-traced lighting works, but the owner saw worse textures than DexNom's. This supersedes every `render` value named above. Don't raise a build above 0.7 (or Belobug above 0.8, DexNom above 0.85) unless the owner asks, and don't describe the pictures of builds at 0.7 as "close to the console" or "near-retail".
+- **Belobug very playable (2026-11-26, owner's call):** later the same day the owner set Belobug to `render: 0.8` (a bit below DexNom's), `fps: 22` (average), `stability: 1` (no crashing), story unchanged at 0.5: 86.1%, #1 in the race ahead of AvatarManz (81.8%) and DexNom (77.4%). Then the owner matched its story progress to CGBJ's, `story: 0.8`: 91.3%, the overall headline leader ahead of CGBJ (89.6%) and NotNozy (87.1%). The owner wanted the card to say it is very playable using about 30 GB of RAM and 12 GB of video memory. Its public README still says "not playable yet" at 5-7 fps and lists about 22 GB of RAM and more video memory than a 16 GB card has; that stays in `blockers` until the README catches up. Keep these values; don't lower them on your own. This supersedes the Belobug `fps`, `stability` and `render` values named above.
